#### \(B\) parameter

Obtained values of Nuclear Slope Parameter and their statistical errors are graphically presented on Figure 3.20. Average value of \(B\) measured by horizontal elastic arms is \(12.71\pm 0.17\) in EHI-WHO and \(12.01\pm 0.24\) in EHO-WHI (given in \(\mathrm{c}^{2}/\mathrm{GeV}^{2}\) unit). These numbers differ by more than 3 standard deviations, what indicate systematic effects to play a significant role. Distinctive is also high spread of values measured with different data sets, as well as variation bewteen arms in the data from the same time period (e.g. set 8), unexplainable within the statistical uncertainties. Sources of these discrepancies are discussed in Chapter 4, and appropriate corrections are derived in Chapter 6.

